1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,732
Welcome to Night 7, the final night of the Cognitive Shutdown Method.

2
00:00:05,682 --> 00:00:08,373
Tonight is about consolidation.

3
00:00:08,373 --> 00:00:12,226
Locking in what worked, and letting go of what did not.

4
00:00:12,226 --> 00:00:15,505
Six nights ago, you started this protocol.

5
00:00:15,505 --> 00:00:17,108
You set an anchor.

6
00:00:17,108 --> 00:00:19,226
You stopped screens early.

7
00:00:19,226 --> 00:00:22,064
You changed what you fueled your body with.

8
00:00:22,064 --> 00:00:24,138
You shaped your environment.

9
00:00:24,138 --> 00:00:26,167
You emptied your mind.

10
00:00:26,167 --> 00:00:28,182
You learned the sequence.

11
00:00:28,182 --> 00:00:31,226
Not all of it worked equally well for you.

12
00:00:31,226 --> 00:00:33,005
That is expected.

13
00:00:33,005 --> 00:00:35,049
Sleep is individual.

14
00:00:35,049 --> 00:00:40,270
Some interventions move the needle for you specifically, and some do less.

15
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:53,417
The research is clear that the people who maintain results over years are the ones who identify their two or three highest-leverage habits and hold those rigid, while letting the others stay flexible.

16
00:00:53,417 --> 00:00:55,932
So tonight, you make a choice.

17
00:00:55,932 --> 00:01:01,241
Of the six interventions, which three made the most difference for your sleep?

18
00:01:01,241 --> 00:01:05,770
Maybe it was the wake time anchor and the brain dump and the cool room.

19
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:11,138
Maybe it was screens off and the constructive worry and the protocol sequence.

20
00:01:11,138 --> 00:01:14,888
Whatever it was, those three become permanent.

21
00:01:14,888 --> 00:01:21,255
The others stay as tools you can return to when sleep slips, and sleep will slip occasionally.

22
00:01:21,255 --> 00:01:23,844
Travel, stress, illness.

23
00:01:23,844 --> 00:01:25,329
Those are normal.

24
00:01:25,329 --> 00:01:28,638
When it happens, you re-run the protocol.

25
00:01:28,638 --> 00:01:32,844
Two or three nights is usually enough to recalibrate.

26
00:01:32,844 --> 00:01:34,844
You are not finished tonight.

27
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:36,329
You are equipped.

28
00:01:36,329 --> 00:01:38,564
The protocol stays with you.

29
00:01:38,564 --> 00:01:42,182
Now, settle into the bed for the last guided night.

30
00:01:42,182 --> 00:01:45,123
Let your body recognize what is coming.

31
00:01:45,123 --> 00:01:48,152
Slow breath in for four seconds.

32
00:01:48,152 --> 00:01:49,755
Hold for seven.

33
00:01:49,755 --> 00:01:51,388
Release for eight.

34
00:01:51,388 --> 00:01:52,564
Again.

35
00:01:52,564 --> 00:01:54,035
In for four.

36
00:01:54,035 --> 00:01:55,638
Hold for seven.

37
00:01:55,638 --> 00:01:57,005
Out for eight.

38
00:01:57,005 --> 00:01:58,564
One last time.

39
00:01:58,564 --> 00:02:00,035
In for four.

40
00:02:00,035 --> 00:02:01,638
Hold for seven.

41
00:02:01,638 --> 00:02:03,005
Out for eight.

42
00:02:03,005 --> 00:02:04,182
You did it.

43
00:02:04,182 --> 00:02:05,520
Sleep well.

